\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Take my life, and let it be
\par Consecrated, Lord, to Thee.
\par Take my moments and my days;
\par Let them flow in ceaseless praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Take my hands, and let them move
\par At the impulse of Thy love.
\par Take my feet, and let them be
\par Swift and beautiful for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Take my voice, and let me sing
\par Always, only for my King.
\par Take my lips, and let them be
\par Filled with messenges from Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Take my silver and my gold;
\par Not a mite would I withhold.
\par Take my intellect, and use
\par Every  power as Thou shalt choose.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Take my will, and make it Thine;
\par It shall be no longer mine.
\par Take my heart- it is Thine own;
\par It shall be Thy royal throne.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Take my love; my Lord, I pour
\par At Thy feet its treasure-store.
\par Take myself, and I will be
\par Ever, only, all for Thee!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

